{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And HaShem was with Joseph.</b> Midrash: Not like the measure of the Holy One, blessed be He, is the measure of flesh and blood. The measure of flesh and blood — as long as he loves his fellow in greatness, he is found with him always; once he falls from his greatness, he casts him behind him. But the Holy One, blessed be He, is not so: He was with him in his greatness and in his descent — in the Egyptian's house He was with him, and when he became ruler and second to the king, there too He was with him, as it is said: ״ויהי ה' את יוסף״; and likewise in the prison: ״ויהי ה' את יוסף ויט אליו חסד״. And similarly, the measure of Joseph is not like that of other people, for a poor man fears Elohim, but a rich man does not fear; yet Joseph, in his master's house, said: ״ואיך אעשה הרעה הגדולה״ etc., and when he was king, said: ״את האלהים אני ירא״. Another interpretation: ״ויהי ה' את יוסף״ — a parable of a man who had ten sons in ten provinces; he left them all and went to the youngest, because his strength was failing and he needed support more than all of them. And another parable: of a man who has ten donkeys laden with wine in the public domain; one of them entered a house of idolatry — he left all his donkeys and went after the one that entered the house of idolatry, so that the wine would not be libated. Thus the Holy One, blessed be He, was with Joseph in the Egyptian's house, so that he would not learn from his deeds."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {0 "ב\"ו read as an abbreviation for בשר ודם (flesh and blood); עכו\"ם resolved as עבודת כוכבים ומזלות (idolatry)."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:06:48.248339469Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}